cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository (or the tr3gpp package) in your research, please
  cite it using the metadata below, and also cite the underlying 3GPP Technical
  Reports themselves — this library provides hand-verified structured extracts,
  not original specification content.
title: >-
  3gpp-tr-library: Hand-verified, section-level 3GPP Technical Reports as
  queryable Markdown, CSV and YAML
abstract: >-
  Hand-curated, section-level extracts of 3GPP Technical Reports, cross-checked
  against multiple independent source formats and published as coordinated
  Markdown, CSV and YAML plus a typed Python API (tr3gpp). Covers TR 38.901
  v19.4.0 clauses 7.4 (pathloss, LOS probability, O2I penetration), 7.5 (fast
  fading), 7.6 (additional modelling components) and 7.9 (ISAC), and TR 36.777
  v15.0.0 Annex B (aerial-UE channel model).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zafari
    given-names: Mehdi
    affiliation: LS-Wireless
repository-code: https://github.com/MehdiZD97/3gpp-tr-library
url: https://github.com/MehdiZD97/3gpp-tr-library
license: MIT
# The Zenodo *concept* DOI: always resolves to the latest archived release, so
# this line does not need updating per release. To cite a specific snapshot,
# use that release's own version DOI from the Zenodo record.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21501655
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
keywords:
  - 3GPP
  - channel model
  - TR 38.901
  - TR 36.777
  - 5G NR
  - wireless propagation
  - pathloss
